## The problems in #4471

Each problem now has a ticket of its own. The counts are the desk's: a report is counted where
the desk files it, and a report the desk read differently is footnoted there.

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>ticket</th><th>problem</th><th>reports</th><th>tenants</th><th>seen</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {#each tickets as t (t.n)}
      <tr><td><a href="{issues}/{t.n}">#{t.n}</a></td><td>{t.problem}</td><td>{t.reports.length}{t.footnote ? ' *' : ''}</td><td>{tenants(t.reports)}</td><td>{seen(t.reports)}</td></tr>
    {/each}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>* {moved} of ticket 1's reports read as a one-day move. They stay counted under ticket 1, where the desk files them by tenant, and ticket 3 holds them as its own problem. {placed} of {merged.length} reports are counted.</p>

### Ticket 1 · the parser

People see the day and the month swap: a booking for 2 December comes out on 12 February. The
shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the day first. This
ticket holds every report the desk files under `parser` by tenant; {moved} of them read as a
one-day move and are footnoted to ticket 3.
[Ticket 1](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

### Ticket 2 · the booking-v3 date hint

These come only through the booking-v3 form, at day-first tenants. The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`
under its date field, people type the month first as it tells them, and the form reads the date
the tenant's way. A parser fix does not close this one: the hint must change. The desk's table
marks this row "no ticket of its own"; now it has one.
[Ticket 2](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

### Ticket 3 · the one-day move

Here the date does not swap; it moves by one day. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says
Monday 11 May." One meeting showed Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. That points at a
date-only value that goes through a time-zone conversion, not at the parser. The desk read these
reports as a one-day move (its notes) and files them under `parser` by tenant, so they were
hidden in that row. [Ticket 3](https://github.com/jexor23/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3).

## How this was counted

- One id, one report. The export comes in pages that overlap, so its {reports.length} rows hold {merged.length} reports.
- The cause comes from the tenant, with the desk's own `causes.ts`, not from intake's tag. Intake guessed from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the tenant on {intakeDisagrees} reports.
- The one-day moves are the reports in the desk's notes (`desk-notes.json`). As the desk counts, they stay counted in the row they are filed under, with a footnote.
- Every number on this page is computed from the export when the page renders.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one bug. The queued parser fix closes ticket 1 only. Ticket 2 needs the booking-v3 hint
changed, and ticket 3 needs the time-zone handling of dates checked.
</Callout>

